WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.060
Snowing, snowing!

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:11.570
Oh, yeah, Nat-chan. I heard you made 
the top four for the All-Japan Junior!

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:13.250
Oh, yeah.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.480
That's your personal best! Congratulations!

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.570
Thanks.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.580
But I lost to Shimizu-san again.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.160
Shimizu-san? That girl from...

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:24.300
Um, sorry for causing you trouble.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.070
I'll be going now.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:27.750
Thank you for your help.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.010
This one was the most frustrating yet.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.760
I was so close...

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.770
Then let's win the All-Japan Junior!

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:47.520
And let's both win and go pro together!

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:49.970
Yeah!

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:22.850
Ten sprints!

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:34.160
The brackets for the Kanagawa Junior came in.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:34.630
Okay.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:40.130
The top sixty-four players from the 
prefectural junior ranking can participate.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:43.590
The sixteen best players get to 
move on to the Kanto Junior,

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.890
the qualifier for the All-Japan Junior.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:50.390
<i>Which means if I win twice, 
I can participate in the Kanto Junior.</i>

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:53.780
<i>I knew I'd need to win 
regardless of who I'd be facing,</i>

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.910
<i>but of all people, and all times...</i>

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:01.410
Maruo Eiichiro

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:01.410
Miyagawa Takuya

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:00.880
<i>Miyagawa-kun, who's seeded third, 
is in the second-round draw...</i>

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:04.350
<i>No, before that, I have to 
think about the first round.</i>

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.700
<i>All the participants in this 
tournament are accomplished players.</i>

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:12.210
<i>And yet there's no data on 
my opponent, Nishimura-kun.</i>

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:12.210
Nishimura Koji

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:19.220
Revenge at the Critical Moment

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:26.310
Araya-san.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.260
Is this "Maruo Eiichiro"

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:31.420
the one who ranked in the top four in 
last year's Kanazawa Junior Circuit?

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:34.390
Yeah, I faced him in the semifinals.

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:36.760
I won, of course.

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:40.170
And he went on to win the STC Cup in the fall.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:44.570
He lost in the first round of the Kanto 
Junior Indoor Invitational in winter.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:47.610
But his opponent was Nabae, after all.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.780
That's not something an unseeded 
player can accomplish so easily.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:53.810
Well, he hasn't competed a lot yet.

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:56.070
What was it like playing against him?

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.840
What type of player is he?

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:01.360
He mainly plays defensively.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:03.880
His serves weren't anything special,

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:07.350
so you'll probably get a chance 
to break without a problem.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:08.520
Right.

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:17.270
You've gotten a lot better.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:20.050
Not yet. I've got a long way to go.

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:21.780
Can we keep going a bit longer?

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:32.470
<i>For me, this will be the challenge of a lifetime.</i>

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:36.420
<i>The battle that will determine 
my future is about to begin.</i>

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:37.660
Hey, Maruo.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:40.210
How are you doing?

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:43.300
That's a huge group you're with.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:47.360
Yeah, we have a lot of participants 
from our club this year.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:48.960
They're mostly underclassmen.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:54.970
Speaking of, are you unseeded this time 
because you weren't in enough tournaments?

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:57.190
Yeah, that's what my coach said.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:00.100
You got a tough draw because of that, huh?

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.600
Miyagawa's in there, too.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:04.010
Yeah, that's right.

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:04.730
Araya-san.

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:07.200
I'm glad I'm on the other side of that block.

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:06.290
Araya-san?

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.290
Hey, Araya-san!

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:09.590
Shut it!

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:11.200
I'm talking here!

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.140
Y-You don't have to get that angry...

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:15.400
That scared me.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.090
Sorry about that.

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:18.460
So, what is it?

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:21.400
Well, isn't this Maruo-san?

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:22.900
Can you introduce us?

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:25.490
Huh? Oh, yeah.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:29.300
This is Nishimura Koji, from our club.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:29.970
Hey.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.940
You two are up against each 
other in the first round, right?

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:34.980
<i>So this is...</i>

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:37.990
I watched your match against 
Araya-san last year.

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:41.530
And I played in the STC Cup, where you won.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:43.600
I was only in the top eight, though.

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:46.280
I'm super interested in those notes of yours!

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:48.450
Anyway, I'm looking forward to our match!

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:52.790
Uh, yes... Looking forward to it, too.

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:55.770
I'm gonna go warm up now.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:00.870
Jeez, he just does whatever 
he wants. Sorry about that.

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.230
<i>As expected from a guy in Araya-kun's club.</i>

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:05.800
But you shouldn't take him lightly.

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:10.720
He hasn't been playing long, but he's 
incredibly athletic, and he's strong-willed.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.310
He's a good fit in our club.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:15.690
He's also grown the fastest.

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:17.100
Huh...

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:21.560
But most importantly, I told him 
about all your weak points!

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:24.390
Wh-What did you tell him?!

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:27.570
Good morning, Araya-kun, Maruo-kun.

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:28.820
Huh?

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:30.770
Miyagawa-kun?!

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:32.320
It's been a while!

00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:33.860
You cut your hair?

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.120
Yeah, chopped it all off.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:39.060
I think you look more mature now.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.310
You think so?

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:43.130
Hmm... So he's the famous Maruo-kun.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:47.010
It's nice to meet you. I'm Mogami Norihiko.

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:50.630
He and I are in the same club.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:51.690
Incidentally...

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:53.320
Whoa, Yukichi-kun?!

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:55.830
He's the second seed here.

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:57.830
Araya-kun is the first seed.

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.520
And Miyagawa is the third seed.

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:00.760
Yep.

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:03.520
In any case, I'm looking 
forward to today, Maruo-kun.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.520
Yeah, me too.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:09.810
Since Takuma-san isn't here, 
we all have a chance this year!

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:11.210
Right, Araya-kun?

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:12.020
Huh?

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:14.660
At the very least, I don't think you've got one.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:16.260
Sure I do!

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:19.370
That's something you say after 
you beat me, the second seed.

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:21.620
Hey, there you are, Ei-chan!

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.420
Oh, Nat-chan!

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:24.920
It's finally time!

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:26.920
Let's do our best!

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:28.920
I'm gonna go register!

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:30.220
'Kay...

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.430
Oh?

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.850
What was that nice mood going on there?

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:37.370
Looks like things are going well for you.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:39.090
Really? Is that what that is?

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:41.990
N-No, uh... I, um...

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:45.130
I-I'm gonna go start warming up!

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:46.540
He ran away.

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:48.440
I know nothing.

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:50.770
<i>Attention, players:</i>

00:07:51.190 --> 00:07:53.160
<i>No. 43, Ishigami-kun,</i>

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:56.450
<i>and No. 44, Nishino-kun, please report to Court 2.</i>

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:58.520
<i>No. 45, Maruo-kun,</i>

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:03.370
<i>and No. 46, Nishimura-kun, please report 
to Court 3 to begin your match.</i>

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:04.460
All right!

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:07.790
<i>I'm not fatigued anymore, thanks 
to the last two days of adjusting.</i>

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:10.070
<i>I ate a solid meal three hours ago,</i>

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:13.180
<i>and I did my full warm-up routine.</i>

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:17.510
<i>Before a match, Nat-chan always 
tells me to try my best.</i>

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:19.520
<i>But today she said, "Let's do our best."</i>

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:24.420
<i>She considers me someone she can 
aim for the nationals with because</i>

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:26.360
<i>she knows how much I've done to get here.</i>

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:30.360
<i>If I lose, I'll have to give up on going pro.</i>

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:33.150
<i>I thought I'd be deathly nervous, but...</i>

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.860
<i>I'm actually calm. That's probably because...</i>

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:39.750
<i>I've done everything I possibly can.</i>

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:45.430
Court 3... Is this where Maruo-kun is?

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:47.380
Yeah, we made it just in time!

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:52.330
<i>Now I just</i>

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:55.380
<i>have to believe in myself and fight!</i>

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:58.890
One-set match. Nishimura to serve.

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:01.140
All right, first serve!

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:04.660
<i>This is a return game for me, 
but I have to play it steady.</i>

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:09.150
<i>Being taken by the opponent's rhythm could 
mean life or death in a one-set match.</i>

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:13.030
<i>First, to avoid risk, use my 1/36 control and...</i>

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:13.690
<i>Go deep!</i>

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:16.110
Out!

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:17.240
Love-15.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:18.620
<i>An error from the get-go?</i>

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:19.690
<i>Why?</i>

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:22.260
<i>Was my ball harder to hit than he expected?</i>

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:24.230
<i>Or is he planning something?</i>

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:27.270
<i>1/36!</i>

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:30.090
<i>How he reacts to this will 
tell me why that happened.</i>

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:31.410
<i>It's short!</i>

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:33.940
<i>The only thing to do with a chance this easy is</i>

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:34.840
<i>score!</i>

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:36.770
Love-30.

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:39.430
<i>Judging by his lack of stability,</i>

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:40.850
<i>it must be both.</i>

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:44.090
<i>He's having trouble returning 
my heavy offensive hits,</i>

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:46.840
<i>and he's also too focused on 
being first, so he's flustered.</i>

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:50.210
<i>A return game, and I'm two points in the lead.</i>

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:52.590
<i>He hasn't overcome it yet.</i>

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:53.570
<i>Which means...</i>

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:56.490
<i>This could already be the turning point!</i>

00:09:57.090 --> 00:09:57.990
<i>All right!</i>

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.480
<i>I won't let this chance slip away.</i>

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:01.010
<i>Go!</i>

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:03.740
<i>He's making a return dash!</i>

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:05.290
<i>He's moving up already?!</i>

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:09.750
Love-40.

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:12.750
<i>Yes! My high-risk offensive 
shot was a success!</i>

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:14.490
<i>Just as I thought.</i>

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:16.840
<i>Maruo-kun's continued to evolve since then.</i>

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:21.070
Game: Maruo. 1-0.

00:10:21.070 --> 00:10:21.970
Yes!

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:23.360
<i>Break!</i>

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:25.090
<i>Now I'm in the lead.</i>

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:28.490
<i>As long as I can hold serve, 
there's no way I can lose!</i>

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:35.110
<i>Even if he breaks my serve this 
game, it'll result in a tie.</i>

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.740
<i>That means...</i>

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:38.150
<i>I can go all-out!</i>

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:42.370
<i>Flex my body like a whip...</i>

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:45.530
15-love.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:49.500
Whoa, that was awesome.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.880
With that body... Are you serious?

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.380
<i>Yes... I'm in good form today!</i>

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:56.380
<i>Y-You've gotta be kidding me!</i>

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:00.520
<i>How are these serves "not anything special"?!</i>

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:02.760
30-love.

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:05.060
<i>What about his play is "defensive"?!</i>

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:07.760
40-love.

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:09.070
<i>A slice now!</i>

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:11.480
<i>His serves aren't just fast, they're varied, too.</i>

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:15.980
<i>His strokes are focused on control, 
but he's still cornering me.</i>

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:18.490
Game: Maruo. 2-0.

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:20.990
<i>This isn't like what I was told at all!</i>

00:11:21.230 --> 00:11:23.990
<i>Okay, 2-0. I can do this.</i>

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:26.990
<i>I'll break here, and go straight for the win!</i>

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:31.620
Game: Maruo. 3-0.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.620
<i>Araya-san, you idiot!</i>

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:35.730
Game: Maruo. 4-0.

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:37.500
<i>You big fat liar!</i>

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:40.160
He's gonna be quite the formidable opponent.

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:41.270
You're right.

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:51.760
Love-15.

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:55.010
<i>Even during our match last year,</i>

00:11:55.010 --> 00:11:56.650
<i>Maruo-kun was trying to change and improve.</i>

00:11:57.210 --> 00:12:00.310
<i>Whereas I just used my clumsiness as an excuse</i>

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:04.660
<i>to keep falling back on my stroke 
while ignoring my shortcomings.</i>

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:07.230
<i>I knew the truth.</i>

00:12:07.230 --> 00:12:11.470
<i>That I needed to improve areas other 
than my stroke in order to get stronger.</i>

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:15.490
<i>Back then, by losing to Maruo-kun, I realized</i>

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:20.440
<i>that I was ignoring my shortcomings 
and not even trying to change.</i>

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:25.850
Game: Maruo. 5-0.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:28.680
<i>At the time, I tried to appear calm and cool.</i>

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:32.010
<i>But inside, the frustration of losing</i>

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:35.690
<i>and the desperate desire to win 
all came surging forth together.</i>

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:40.090
<i>Even I was surprised at how 
intense my feelings were.</i>

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:45.700
<i>From then on, I tried numerous different 
ways to change how I played tennis.</i>

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:49.420
<i>Since I'm a defensive baseliner, 
I practiced different shots that would</i>

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:51.720
<i>bring me toward the net, but...</i>

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:53.240
<i>It didn't work out very well.</i>

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:00.130
Go in!

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:03.930
Game, set, and match.

00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:03.930
Damn it!

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:04.970
Winner: Ikemoto.

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:07.900
Score: 6-3, 7-5.

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:08.970
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:30.370
<i>It's no good.</i>

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:41.190
Oobayashi-senpai...

00:13:43.490 --> 00:13:44.880
What's wrong?

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:48.160
Lately, you haven't been playing like yourself,

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:49.640
and it's ruining your game.

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:51.650
Are you trying to change your playing style?

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:54.700
No matter what I try, it doesn't work.

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:58.660
I guess it's not that easy to find a new weapon...

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:03.240
I'm starting to think this was 
too high a hurdle for me.

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:07.460
Maybe... it's better that I give up...

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:14.400
Hey, Miyagawa.

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:19.070
You know, I gave up in the end.

00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:25.710
I'm in my third year of high school, 
so I was thinking about my future.

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:30.400
I did want to go pro, if only slightly.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:35.310
But I gave up on that completely, 
and decided to go to college

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:38.240
and think about my future 
while continuing to playing tennis.

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:43.480
I didn't have the skills to rank among 
the top players in Kanagawa, after all.

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:46.440
So wanting to go pro was 
a little presumptuous.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:47.510
That's not true!

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:51.090
But you have the skill,

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:53.740
and you still have plenty of time 
to reach for your dreams.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:57.250
Do your absolute best for another year.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:00.120
I don't think you're wrong to

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:02.820
practice your volleys so you 
can overcome your weak point.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:07.020
But your strokes are top notch.

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:10.260
I think it's worth it to make 
better use of that stroke.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:17.770
Oobayashi-senpai...

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:26.050
Senpai...

00:15:29.270 --> 00:15:33.310
<i>I want to see results from the training 
I've done for this past year.</i>

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:34.520
<i>For that to happen,</i>

00:15:34.520 --> 00:15:36.280
<i>I have to defeat Maruo-kun!</i>

00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:42.600
Nishimura

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:39.920
Game, set, and match.

00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:42.580
Winner: Maruo. Score: 6-0.

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:44.470
Yes! Maruo-kun did it!

00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:46.090
Yeah, he bageled him!

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:50.670
<i>Well, he's gotta be able to do that much.</i>

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:52.100
Congratulations!

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:54.180
You didn't even break a sweat!

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:05.190
Maruo

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:05.190
Nishino Akira

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:01.610
Hey, Ei-chan!

00:16:01.610 --> 00:16:03.430
Miyagawa-kun's match is starting!

00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:05.190
Okay, I'll be right there!

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:07.190
How's the match?

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:09.440
Love-30.

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:12.530
Wow, as expected from the beast of strokes!

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:14.200
<i>According to last year's data...</i>

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:23.460
Speciality: Multiple Stroke Types
Spin, Side Spin, Top Spin, Slice, Side Slice, Cut, Flat

00:16:14.430 --> 00:16:19.250
<i>His height gave him powerful ambidextrous 
forehand and backhand strokes.</i>

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:23.460
<i>He had seven different full-swing 
strokes that rarely missed.</i>

00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:26.960
<i>He must've learned something 
new within the last year.</i>

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:29.670
Love-40.

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:30.660
Yes!

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:32.720
<i>But as of now, I don't see any huge changes.</i>

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:36.220
<i>His strokes themselves have clearly 
improved, but other than that...</i>

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:39.620
Game: Miyagawa. 4-0.

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:43.300
<i>Their difference in strength 
ends it too quickly...</i>

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:44.720
Hey, Maruo-kun!

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:47.700
It's been a while. How are you?

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:48.980
Oh, hey!

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:50.190
Who's that?

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:52.470
He's the first person Ei-chan 
ever played against.

00:16:53.140 --> 00:16:55.220
Are you here to support Miyagawa-kun?

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:56.470
Yep!

00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:59.650
And I have a few other 
underclassmen here, too.

00:16:59.650 --> 00:17:00.770
Like Mogami.

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:05.410
I got accepted to university, 
so I'm rather free nowadays.

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:07.260
You're done with entrance exams?

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:10.250
Well, it was more an athletic 
referral than an exam.

00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:13.290
Last year, I had trouble deciding what to do,

00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:15.760
but this seems like the right choice.

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:17.760
<i>I had no idea.</i>

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:21.040
By the way, I saw the tournament bracket.

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:23.270
Miyagawa's looking pretty good, too.

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:25.070
If he keeps this up, 
you'll face him next.

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:25.760
Yeah.

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:30.270
I'd better put some effort into 
cheering Miyagawa on this year.

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:34.280
He was so frustrated when 
he lost to you last year.

00:17:36.190 --> 00:17:39.280
Oh, no, that was like a miracle, really...

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:43.540
But the way Miyagawa's playing today, 
he'll be pretty tough to beat.

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:47.160
If he can't move on to the 
Kanto Junior from here,

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:49.890
he has to start reconsidering his future.

00:17:49.890 --> 00:17:51.040
His future?

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:53.110
Well, of course.

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:57.050
I think the All-Japan Junior is a huge 
deciding factor for a lot of players.

00:17:58.060 --> 00:18:02.050
It measures how you rank 
against your generation,

00:18:02.050 --> 00:18:04.530
and the outcome has a huge 
influence on players' futures.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:07.060
Everyone's got a lot riding on this.

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:09.060
Miyagawa's no exception.

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:11.560
Which is why, this time,

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:13.780
he'll come at you with all he's got.

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:19.620
Game, set, and match.

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:22.330
Winner: Miyagawa. Score: 6-0.

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:24.830
Looks like you have your opponent.

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:35.930
<i>I can't let my body cool off or tire 
too much before the second match.</i>

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:40.760
<i>I have to give up on going 
pro if I lose today, too.</i>

00:18:41.420 --> 00:18:45.650
<i>I wonder if this is how Araya-kun 
felt facing Takuma-san last year.</i>

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:49.770
<i>From this point on, everyone's 
future will be on the line.</i>

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:54.840
<i>I've done all I could because I knew 
I needed to win matches like that, right?</i>

00:18:57.240 --> 00:18:58.220
Hey, you!

00:18:58.220 --> 00:18:59.210
Y-Yes?!

00:18:59.210 --> 00:19:02.200
You have a scary look on your face.

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:04.660
It doesn't matter how scary your face looks.

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:06.520
Your opponent won't be intimidated.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:09.350
That's not why I look like this!

00:19:09.350 --> 00:19:10.160
Listen.

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:13.960
Anyone in your position 
would be a little nervous.

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:19.010
But remember that in the end, the one who 
enjoys their time the most is the winner.

00:19:19.370 --> 00:19:20.510
Right.

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:23.610
Also remember that before you met me,

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:26.740
even if it was a miracle, you beat Miyagawa.

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:30.520
How much do you think we've 
accomplished since you met me?

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:33.250
Just thinking about it logically, 
there's no way you could lose.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:39.030
<i>No. 45, Maruo-kun, and No. 48, Miyagawa-kun,</i>

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:42.240
<i>please report to Court 6 to begin your match.</i>

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:45.960
It's finally time. Go win it, Ei-chan.

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:46.730
Yeah.

00:19:46.730 --> 00:19:49.290
Go secure your spot in the Kanto Junior!

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:50.610
Right!

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:03.300
I'll get my revenge today.

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:05.800
Yeah. I won't lose, either.

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:07.810
Good luck!

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:10.310
One-set match.

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:12.330
Maruo to serve.

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:15.810
<i>He's on a totally different level 
from my first round opponent.</i>

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:19.240
<i>If my game is too steady, 
I'll be cornered by his stroke.</i>

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:24.360
<i>I'll go into the second round at 
full throttle right from the start!</i>

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:28.720
15-love.

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:31.660
<i>His serve is even faster than 
it was in his first round.</i>

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:33.990
<i>That speed with that physique...</i>

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:38.420
<i>He made fast serves his weapon by figuring 
out how to use his body and flexibility.</i>

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:42.670
<i>To think he turned his past weakness 
into a weapon this powerful.</i>

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:44.420
<i>That was too close.</i>

00:20:44.420 --> 00:20:47.460
<i>If this were the first round, 
that would've easily been an ace.</i>

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:52.430
<i>Looks like I should try out different 
shots before he gets used to my speed.</i>

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:55.540
<i>Then, next, I'll go for a slice down the center!</i>

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:57.690
<i>It's not fast...</i>

00:20:58.050 --> 00:20:59.690
<i>But it's getting away from me!</i>

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:06.460
Out. 30-love.

00:21:06.920 --> 00:21:08.620
<i>He hit it back one-handed!</i>

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:10.720
<i>And it was incredibly accurate...</i>

00:21:10.720 --> 00:21:15.030
<i>Since he has long limbs, he already had 
a wider range of coverage than most.</i>

00:21:15.030 --> 00:21:18.630
<i>So now that coverage area 
is a step wider on each side?</i>

00:21:19.050 --> 00:21:23.340
<i>Which means that slower serves will 
have a higher chance of being returned.</i>

00:21:23.830 --> 00:21:26.660
<i>I'm feeling confident today, 
so let's go with a flat serve.</i>

00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:31.080
<i>Damn, I put too much power into it.</i>

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:33.790
<i>No, a flat serve is riskier than other serves.</i>

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:35.570
<i>Focus and move onto the second serve.</i>

00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:38.930
<i>Make up for the reduced 
speed with solid aim, and...</i>

00:21:38.930 --> 00:21:39.610
<i>Spin!</i>

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:41.770
<i>Here it comes!</i>

00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:42.900
<i>A powerful flat shot!</i>

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:44.780
<i>Moving up?!</i>

00:21:45.750 --> 00:21:48.090
<i>A defensive baseliner like
Miyagawa-kun is moving up!</i>

00:21:48.090 --> 00:21:49.780
<i>But this is all expected!</i>

00:21:50.230 --> 00:21:54.980
<i>Now it comes down to Miyagawa-kun's 
volley and my practiced footwork!</i>

00:21:56.710 --> 00:21:57.290
<i>Here it comes!</i>

00:22:08.190 --> 00:22:09.800
30-15.

00:22:10.240 --> 00:22:12.610
<i>A d-drive volley?!</i>

00:22:27.380 --> 00:22:31.390
<i>This is my new weapon that's 
going to help me change!</i>

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:25.060
Next Time

00:24:00.450 --> 00:24:01.680
Maruo-kun is amazing

00:24:01.680 --> 00:24:04.380
to be able to evolve his tennis 
this far in such a short time.

00:24:04.380 --> 00:24:07.090
I should consider him a different 
person from who he was last year.

00:24:07.090 --> 00:24:09.340
Miyagawa-kun is as strong as I expected.

00:24:09.590 --> 00:24:11.170
My condition for going pro,

00:24:11.540 --> 00:24:13.500
a win at the All-Japan Junior...

00:24:13.500 --> 00:24:18.170
I absolutely have to win this 
match in order to get there!

00:24:18.170 --> 00:24:21.350
In a match like this, there's 
no telling what will happen!

00:24:21.350 --> 00:24:22.980
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.580 --> 00:24:25.060
The Speed of Evolution

00:24:22.980 --> 00:24:24.420
"The Speed of Evolution."

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:31.000
End
